          body: `Matching values can be interesting, but the next step should always be comparison rather than conclusion. Check alternate spellings, abbreviations, or transliterations first. Two names may land on the same total while coming from very different structures, which means the shared number is only the beginning of the conversation.\n\nIt also helps to compare the names with the words that sit around them. If a name shares a value with a cluster of related ideas, titles, or traits, that broader field may tell you more than the raw number alone. In contrast, if the match stands by itself with no supporting context, it may be less useful for interpretation.\n\nThe most reliable approach is to use the name lookup page for quick comparisons and then record the strongest companion words you find. That creates a balanced view built from value, structure, and context.`,
